// The Campaign (GDD, section 4): region 1, Plain of Menhirs (stages 1-20, no battle rule: teaches the basics);
// region 2, Drowned Archipelago (21-40, mostly Water: elements and effects, boss at 40); region 3, Citadel of the
// Broken Seal (41-50, Light and Dark, boss at 50). Difficulty rises from gentle to hard: the reference team of
// each stage (Tests/ReferenceTeams.AtCampaign) wins ~97% of the first ten, ~92% up to 25, ~90% to ~78% up to 35 (the
// reference farm point, Faimon: enemies 6 stars level 40, 12,100 XP per monster) and ~78% to ~38% at 50, while the experience per victory is highest early
// and lowest at the end (Tests: dotnet run --project Tests -- --simulate; docs/ESTUDO_XP_E_CAMPANHA.md).
// Enemies at the stage stars and level ("stars", "level"): "summon" is a summon variant from Data/summons (buffed for the fight),
// "enemy" a unique creature from Data/enemies.json with its "element". "scale" multiplies the enemies' HP and Attack,
// "attackScale" and "speedScale" their Attack and Speed again (the level/attack/speed curve that makes late stages hard):
// they are the calibration of each stage, so that heavier waves don't need a level that lies about them.
// First-clear prizes (Core/Progression/Milestones, VictoryReward.BonusRunes): "firstClearScrolls" are Mystic Scrolls;
// "firstClearRunes" Legendary runes at the stage stars (they replace half of the Mystic Scrolls); "firstClearKits" a
// kit of six Legendary 6-star runes with the set of the player's choice (stage 20); "firstClearLegendary" Legendary
// Scrolls (stage 40); "firstClearLightDark" a Light and Dark Scroll (stage 50); "firstClearCores" Infusion Cores.
// "mana" is the cost of each victory (a defeat costs nothing). Scrolls only on the first victory; Essence and
// experience on every victory. The experience is a pool for the team: it is split among the monsters present
// (Leveling.Share, a full team gives "experience" to each monster: 4 on the maps; fewer give more to each); the account gets "experience" whole.
// The rune (up to 4 stars) always drops on the first victory and with a 50% chance on later ones. 5 and 6 star
// runes and the tools come from the Dungeons (Data/dungeons.json).
